WEBVTT

00:06:55.579 --> 00:07:00.163
If they look you up and they find out
you are really into some bad stuff,

00:07:00.579 --> 00:07:04.079
sometimes that's the end of it. They're
just going to pass on you.

00:07:04.871 --> 00:07:08.163
Aaron coaches his students to call
out the elephant in the room.

00:07:08.413 --> 00:07:11.454
I made some very poor decisions.
I've paid for that.

00:07:11.454 --> 00:07:13.371
I've made a lot of changes in my life.

00:07:13.579 --> 00:07:16.121
I would really appreciate
the opportunity.

00:07:16.329 --> 00:07:17.788
Why do you think it's important, Aaron,

00:07:17.788 --> 00:07:21.371
to address the elephant in the room and
actually talk about it directly?

00:07:22.246 --> 00:07:24.204
The number one thing is you control

00:07:24.204 --> 00:07:26.454
the narrative to some degree
when you do that.

00:07:29.288 --> 00:07:30.663
Controlling the narrative,